// P4: positive lower-bound guard proves division safety.
// The condition d > 0 leaves d in [1, 3], which the interval domain CAN
// represent; the division is then provably safe (no alarm, no concrete
// fault).  Contrast with p3: the form of the guard matters for intervals.
input d;
var q = 0;
if (d > 0) {
  q = 100 / d;
}
